{"name":"Fire Flower","hex":"#f68f37","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fire","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A (usually self-sustaining) chemical reaction involving the bonding of oxygen with carbon or other fuel, with the production of heat and the presence of flame or smouldering.","An instance of this chemical reaction, especially when intentionally created and maintained in a specific location to a useful end (such as a campfire or a hearth fire)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Amazing; excellent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fire"},{"term":"flower","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colorful, conspicuous structure associated with angiosperms, frequently scented and attracting various insects, and which may or may not be used for sexual reproduction.","A reproductive structure in angiosperms (flowering plants), often conspicuously colourful and typically including sepals, petals, and either or both stamens and/or a pistil."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put forth blooms.","To decorate with pictures of flowers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flower"}],"entries":[{"title":"Super Mario","blocks":[{"text":"Super Mario is a platform game series developed and published by Nintendo and starring their mascot, Mario. The series was created by Japanese game designer Shigeru Miyamoto and is the flagship series of the greater Mario franchise. At least one Super Mario game has been released for every major Nintendo video game console. A limited number of Super Mario games have also released on non-Nintendo gaming platforms."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Mario"},{"title":"Fire","blocks":[{"text":"Fire is the rapid oxidation of a fuel in the exothermic chemical process of combustion, releasing heat, light, and various reaction products.\nFlames, the most visible portion of the fire, are produced in the combustion reaction when the fuel reaches its ignition point temperature. Flames from hydrocarbon fuels consist primarily of carbon dioxide, water vapor, oxygen, and nitrogen. If hot enough, the gases may become ionized to produce plasma. The color and intensity of the flame depend on the type of fuel and composition of the surrounding gases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Large_bonfire.jpg/330px-Large_bonfire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire"},{"title":"Flower","blocks":[{"text":"Flowers, also known as blossoms and blooms, are the reproductive structures of flowering plants. Typically, they are structured in four circular levels around the end of a stalk. These include: sepals, which are modified leaves that support the flower; petals, often designed to attract pollinators; male stamens, where pollen is presented; and female gynoecia, where pollen is received and its movement is facilitated to the egg. When flowers are arranged in a group, they are known collectively as an inflorescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg/330px-Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/50/NES_Super_Mario_Bros.png/250px-NES_Super_Mario_Bros.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/50/NES_Super_Mario_Bros.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/50/NES_Super_Mario_Bros.png/250px-NES_Super_Mario_Bros.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The 2D Super Mario games are known for their side-scrolling gameplay, seen here in the first level of Super Mario Bros. (1985), the series' first game.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANES_Super_Mario_Bros.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/61/Supermushroom.png/250px-Supermushroom.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/61/Supermushroom.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/61/Supermushroom.png/250px-Supermushroom.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"UGO described the Super Mushroom item as \"the quintessential power-up\".[7]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASupermushroom.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Takashi_Tezuka%2C_Shigeru_Miyamoto_and_K%C5%8Dji_Kond%C5%8D.jpg/500px-Takashi_Tezuka%2C_Shigeru_Miyamoto_and_K%C5%8Dji_Kond%C5%8D.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Takashi_Tezuka%2C_Shigeru_Miyamoto_and_K%C5%8Dji_Kond%C5%8D.jpg/1280px-Takashi_Tezuka%2C_Shigeru_Miyamoto_and_K%C5%8Dji_Kond%C5%8D.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Takashi_Tezuka%2C_Shigeru_Miyamoto_and_K%C5%8Dji_Kond%C5%8D.jpg/500px-Takashi_Tezuka%2C_Shigeru_Miyamoto_and_K%C5%8Dji_Kond%C5%8D.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Development of Super Mario Bros. was led by Shigeru Miyamoto (center) and Takashi Tezuka (left), while Koji Kondo (right) served as composer.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATakashi_Tezuka%2C_Shigeru_Miyamoto_and_K%C5%8Dji_Kond%C5%8D.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/SNES-Mod1-Console-Set.jpg/500px-SNES-Mod1-Console-Set.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pa